mdv: "1.0"
title: Matrix data
---

# Deliveries by depot and day

A matrix is written as the grid a reader wants to look at and read as the
long table an encoder can bind: every cell becomes its own record of `row`,
`column`, and `value`. Two depots across three days are six rows, and the
field names are always those three — the corner cell says `depot`, and that
word is a label for the reader that no channel can name.

Wednesday at the northern depot has not been counted yet. An empty cell is
a cell that exists and is empty, so the record is kept and its value reads
null rather than the row going missing.

```mdv heatmap
title: Deliveries by depot and day
format: matrix
---
| depot | Mon | Tue | Wed |
| ----- | --- | --- | --- |
| north | 12  | 18  |     |
| south | 7   | 9   | 14  |
```
